  era: "6th c. BCE \xB7 Section 5 \xB7 Mahajanapadas \xB7 c. 600 \u2013 321 BCE"
  title: Monarchies
  text: Most mahajanapadas, such as Magadha, Kosala, Vatsa and Avanti, were monarchies. Kings collected taxes, kept armies and officials, and built fortified capitals such as Rajagriha, Shravasti, Kaushambi and Ujjain.
